==Old English==

===Etymology===
From Germanic: cognate with Old Saxon [[thunkian]] (Dutch [[dunken]]), Old High German [[thunken]] (German [[dünken]]), Old Norse [[þykkja]] (Swedish [[tycka]]), Gothic [[𐌸𐌿𐌲𐌺𐌾𐌰𐌽]], Limburgish [[tönk]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈθynʧɑn/|lang=ang}}

===Verb===
'''þynċan'''

# {{impersonal|lang=ang}} to [[seem]], [[appear]] (''+ dative'')

